# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DE COMPLETENESS — WAVE 1 (rev 2026-08-01)
# docs/DE_COMPLETENESS_AND_EDITIONS_2026-07-31.md §2.1
# Every entry here backs something that was already built, shipped and
# exposed in Settings but could not run for want of a package.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# gtk4-layer-shell — the GTK4 layer-shell binding.
# /opt/nyxus/desktop/nyxus_desktop.py is a complete GTK4 layer-shell desktop
# client (wallpaper paint per-monitor at the BOTTOM layer + right-click →
# nyxus-context-menu.sh). It does gi.require_version("Gtk4LayerShell","1.0")
# and this profile only ever listed `gtk-layer-shell`, which is the GTK **3**
# library and a different package. The import guard's fallback is
# os.execvp("swaybg", …) with a message on stderr nobody reads, so the desktop
# layer degraded to a plain wallpaper with no right-click and NO visible error.
gtk4-layer-shell

# loupe — image viewer. There was no image viewer on the ISO at all, so every
# PNG/JPEG resolved to Firefox (which claims those types) and opened in a
# browser tab. Needed before a mimeapps.list has anything to point at.
loupe

# zathura + zathura-pdf-mupdf — PDF viewer, same story: no PDF reader shipped,
# so application/pdf fell through to Firefox. The -pdf-mupdf plugin is what
# actually renders PDF; zathura alone opens nothing.
zathura
zathura-pdf-mupdf

# qt5ct + qt6ct — Qt theming, and the ONE consistent option available.
# skel already ships ~/.config/qt5ct/qt5ct.conf and ~/.config/qt6ct/qt6ct.conf
# (style=Fusion + the custom nyxus-prism ALIEN NEON palette) and NEITHER
# package was installed, so nothing read either file and every Qt app rendered
# default light grey.
#
# The DE study's §2.1 item 3 asked for `adwaita-qt5` + `adwaita-qt6` instead
# (to match QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=adwaita-dark in /etc/environment.d). Those
# packages NO LONGER EXIST in the Arch repos — `pacman -Si adwaita-qt5` and
# `adwaita-qt6` both resolve to nothing on a fully synced box (upstream
# adwaita-qt is archived), and pacstrap ABORTS on an unknown package, so
# listing them would have failed the bake outright. qt5ct/qt6ct is the
# alternative the study itself offers in §1.3 row 7, and it is the better one
# because the config it needs is already in skel and already on palette.
qt5ct
qt6ct

# ffmpegthumbnailer — video thumbnails in Files. Image thumbnails already work
# (nautilus pulls glycin); video and PDF had none. `tumbler` is deliberately
# NOT added — it serves the thunar family, and no thunar-family file manager
# ships here.
ffmpegthumbnailer

# ── DE completeness Wave 2 · the MIME substrate (§2.2) ────────────────────
# Both of these were ALREADY on the ISO, and both only by accident. Listing
# them explicitly is the whole point: the accidents are load-bearing and one of
# them breaks the moment a lighter edition drops a browser.
#
# xdg-utils — xdg-open and xdg-mime themselves, i.e. the mechanism the entire
# mimeapps.list depends on. It reached the image only because CHROMIUM
# hard-depends on it. The daily edition planned in
# DAILY_DRIVER_PRODUCT_BRIEF_2026-08-01.md drops chromium, and the existing
# packages.x86_64.lean tier already does — which means that tier has no
# xdg-open and no xdg-mime at all, and nothing opens anything by association.
xdg-utils
# xdg-user-dirs — ~/Documents, ~/Downloads, ~/Pictures and friends. Reached
# only transitively via nautilus → xdg-user-dirs-gtk, and the firstboot
# fragment that called xdg-user-dirs-update did so as root with `|| true`, so
# a break in that chain silently left the user with a bare home directory.
xdg-user-dirs

