# ── NYXUS Tier C (rev 2026-05-14): security & network polish ───────
# usbguard already shipped above (line 377). Adding strongSwan plug-in,
# Secure Boot manager (sbctl), TPM2 userspace tools, MAC randomizer,
# and dnscrypt-proxy for DNS-over-HTTPS.
#
# IMPORTANT: usbguard daemon ships with PresentDevicePolicy=allow and
# an EMPTY rules.conf so it never locks the user out of their own USB
# keyboard at install time. Per user pref: account-lockout / hardening
# policies are opt-in post-install only. UsbPage exposes the toggle.
networkmanager-strongswan
sbctl
tpm2-tools
macchanger
dnscrypt-proxy
sound-theme-freedesktop
qt5-svg

# ── NYXUS Ghost / Invisibility mode (rev 2026-07-17) ───────────────
# tor + torsocks back nyxus-ghost (invisibility/anonymity mode): the
# script toggles a Tor transparent proxy + nftables egress kill-switch,
# randomises the MAC (macchanger, above), and mutes mDNS (avahi). tor is
# TOGGLED by nyxus-ghost — its service is deliberately NOT enabled at boot
# (see customize_airootfs.sh: tor.service is absent from the enable list).
# nftables (Bifrost dep, above) provides the kill-switch ruleset.
tor
torsocks

# ── NYXUS greeter stack (rev 2026-07-14) — REQUIRED ────────────────
# The ISO enables greetd (see customize_airootfs.sh). The greeter chain
# nyxus-greeter runs regreet under cage, falling back to tuigreet (text).
# Without these three the ISO boots to greetd with NO greeter binary =
# broken login. cage/regreet are Wayland (dodges the SDDM X11 hybrid-GPU
# crash). SDDM is intentionally NOT installed anymore.
greetd-regreet
greetd-tuigreet
cage

