# ── NYXUS Master Hub (Bifrost) runtime deps (rev 2026-07-15) ───────
# Bifrost is the Tauri-based security dashboard staged into airootfs by
# build-iso.sh (binary already built off-tree at ~/Projects/bifrost).
# webkit2gtk-4.1/gtk3/libayatana-appindicator are required for the Tauri
# window + tray icon to render at all; the python-* set covers the
# guardian.py sidecar's imports.
#
# ★ CORRECTED 2026-07-27: ollama IS now listed. The previous note said it was
# "intentionally NOT listed - guardian.py already degrades gracefully without
# it (logs a non-fatal warning)". That assumption was WRONG and was measured
# on the live box: with ollama absent, heimdall.guardian gets
# [Errno 111] Connection refused on EVERY event, which means
#   CircuitBreaker guardian_extractor: OPEN   (permanently)
#   [!] AI queue full - dropped suspicious event   ~15,000 per hour
#   every verdict downgraded to action=LOG effective=LOG severity=INFO
# That is not graceful degradation - it is silent blindness, and the unit
# still reports `active` the whole time. Shipping ollama means a fresh
# install has a working AI EDR instead of one that only looks alive.
#
# NOTE the MODEL is not baked (941M): first boot still needs
#   ollama pull qwen2.5:1.5b-instruct     (or run: nyxus-edr-repair)
ollama
# suricata: host wire visibility. nyxus-suricata-setup ships in
# /usr/local/bin but the package did not, so on a fresh install the script
# had to pull it at runtime. The honeypots only see traffic aimed at the
# bait; nothing watched what actually crosses the NIC. Shipping it means
# `nyxus-suricata-setup` works offline on first boot.
suricata
webkit2gtk-4.1
gtk3
libayatana-appindicator
python-pydantic
python-openai
python-aiohttp
sqlite
nftables

# ── Meli (Honeypot Command Center) runtime deps (rev 2026-07-16) ──────
# Meli app + venv staged into airootfs by build-iso.sh from the installed
# /opt/meli (see PKGBUILD/install.sh). gtk4/libadwaita/python-gobject/
# python-cryptography/python-requests/python-bcrypt are already listed
# above for other NYXUS components; only the deps unique to Meli's
# PKGBUILD `depends=()` are added here. The shipped venv uses
# --system-site-packages, so these must be real pacman packages, not
# just pip installs baked into the venv.
