# ── jeTT AI Security Daemon runtime deps (rev 2026-07-16) ─────────────
# jett-daemon itself is a self-contained Rust binary (ldd shows only
# libc/libgcc/libm — no extra runtime packages needed there); GPU
# inference depends on the nvidia-open-dkms/nvidia-utils/opencl-nvidia
# already listed above for the rest of NYXUS.

# ── honeypot/Docker stack runtime deps (rev 2026-07-16, r2) ────────────
# Needed to run the pre-pulled cowrie/conpot/dionaea/endlessh/heralding/
# http-honeypot + grafana/prometheus/loki/promtail containers staged into
# /opt/honeypot by build-iso.sh. `docker-compose` on Arch ships both the
# standalone binary AND the `docker compose` CLI plugin, so either
# invocation style works. iptables (already listed above) covers the
# DOCKER-USER egress-lockdown firewall.
docker
docker-compose

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BLACKARCH — curated offensive/defensive toolkit (rev 2026-07-17)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The [blackarch] repo is wired in nyx-profile/pacman.conf; the host
# keyring (blackarch-keyring, populated on this build box) verifies these
# at pacstrap, and customize_airootfs.sh populates the keyring + adds the
# repo to the LIVE /etc/pacman.conf so post-boot installs keep working.
#
# SIZE TRADEOFF (documented per the task): the full `blackarch` group is
# ~2800 packages and would balloon the ISO to tens of GB. Instead this is
# a CURATED ~67-tool set spanning recon / scanner / webapp / exploitation /
# wireless / cracker / forensic / anti-forensic / sniffer / proxy / crypto —
# enough to be "loaded with the works" while the ISO still bakes + boots
# (adds roughly a few GB, dominated by metasploit/zaproxy/kismet). Anyone
# who wants EVERYTHING runs `nyxus-blackarch-full` post-boot (installs the
# whole `blackarch` group). Tools already shipped from official repos
# (nmap, wireshark-cli, radare2, rizin, ghidra, binwalk, yara, sleuthkit,
# volatility3, tcpdump, gdb, tor, torsocks, macchanger, …) are NOT relisted
# here to avoid duplicates.
# NOTE: blackarch package names are curated by hand; if any single name
# fails to resolve at the first real bake, remove that one line (pacstrap
# aborts on an unknown package) — everything else is independent.

# ── keyring + mirrorlist (so the LIVE system trusts + resolves blackarch)
blackarch-keyring
blackarch-mirrorlist

